  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcome (minimum probability event) and prefers the one with the higher payoff. The individual considers the lower probability of success but chooses for the sake of a higher gain, which aligns with focusing on the most favorable but least likely outcome. The verbal report reflects a preference for a higher reward despite lower likelihood, which matches the core logic of the decision reason. Although the report does not explicitly mention comparing the least probable outcomes, the justification—choosing a lower chance for a higher gain—mirrors the reasoning pattern of preferring the more favorable rare outcome. The emphasis on 'higher gain despite lower probability' strongly suggests use of the same consideration as the decision reason.",
